<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the League of Cognac</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1526">1526</a>–<a href="/years/1530">1530</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-wars">Italian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the League of Cognac was fought from 1526 to 1530 between Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> and an alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-clement-vii">Pope Clement VII</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> formed to limit <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Imperial troops sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 1527, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-cambrai">Peace of Cambrai</a> (1529) and the fall of Florence (1530) left Charles dominant in Italy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-league-of-cognac.jpg" alt="War of the League of Cognac" width="320" height="170" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giorgio Vasari · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siege_of_Florence.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
